course: dictionary
lesson: 4098
title: Moving with care
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words show how someone does something. «She stepped gingerly onto the ice.» Gingerly tells you how she stepped: slowly and carefully, because she was afraid the ice might crack or that she might slip.
explain: The clues are the words around it. Ice is slippery and can break, so a careful, slow step makes sense. Try the swap: "She stepped carefully onto the ice" means nearly the same, so gingerly means very carefully.
explain: Gingerly is also used when something might hurt. «Mole steps gingerly into the boat» shows Mole is not sure it is safe, so he moves with care. Authors choose gingerly to show caution, not just slowness.
fact: Gingerly means very carefully and slowly, because you are afraid of hurting yourself or breaking something.
fact: Gingerly is mostly an adverb, a word that tells how an action is done.
fact: Gingerly can also be an adjective, but this is less common.
fact: «Gingerly» is often used for moving near danger, such as ice, or touching something sore.
fact: Carefully is a close synonym, but gingerly suggests you are a bit afraid of what might happen.
exercise: «She stepped gingerly onto the ice.» What does gingerly mean here? | Quickly and loudly | Happily, skipping along | *Very carefully, in case it cracks or slips | Angrily, stamping her feet
exercise: «Mole steps gingerly into the boat.» Why might Mole move this way? | *He is not sure the boat is safe | He is too happy to notice the boat | He is in a hurry to get home | He wants to make a loud splash
exercise: Which word is closest in meaning to gingerly? | *Carefully | Boldly | Noisily | Rapidly
test: «Alice goes gingerly near strange creatures.» What does gingerly show about Alice? | *She is cautious and a little worried about being hurt | She is very excited and runs straight at them | She is fast asleep | She is bored and wants to leave
test: Which sentence uses gingerly correctly? | *She lifted the cracked vase gingerly, so it would not break | He shouted gingerly across the field | The dog barked gingerly at the postman | The sun shone gingerly all day
exam: Gingerly is usually an adverb, so what job does it do in a sentence? | It describes a noun, like a colour | It names a person, place or thing | It joins two sentences together | *It tells you how an action is done
